      "published_at": "2026-10-19T14:00:00+00:00",
      "snippet": "In the third quarter of 2026 (3Q26), 23% of new light-duty vehicles sold in the United States were hybrid electric, battery electric, or plug-in hybrid electric vehicles, down slightly from 24% in 3Q25. Between 3Q25 and 3Q26, hybrid electric vehicles continued to gain market share, reaching 16% of light-duty vehicle sales. Growth of hybrid electric vehicle sales has slowed this quarter as the average transaction price for a new vehicle passed $50,000-the first time this price has been reached so",
      "source": "U.S. EIA Today in Energy",
      "title": "Hybrid sales rise while battery electric sales remain lower after tax credit expiration",
      "url": "https://www.eia.gov/todayinenergy/detail.php?id=68325"
